course: dictionary
lesson: 8474
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. To pick the right one, read the sentence around the word. The words around it are its context, and they tell you which meaning fits.
explain: «The Salvation Army was founded in London by William and Catherine Booth.» Here Salvation is part of a name, so the sentence is about a church and a charity, not about a rescue.
explain: Salvation can also mean anything that saves you from danger, trouble or failure. «The bus was my salvation in the rain.» Nobody is talking about a church here: the bus rescued the writer from getting soaked. Put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Salvation is a noun you cannot count, like water or happiness.
fact: In Christianity, salvation means being saved from sin and its results.
fact: Christians believe Jesus brings salvation, so that people can be close to God for ever.
fact: The Salvation Army is a Christian church and charity. It was founded in London by William and Catherine Booth.
fact: Its motto of care is often put as «soup, soap and salvation», and it is famous for helping the poor.
exercise: «The Salvation Army was founded in London by William and Catherine Booth.» Where was the Salvation Army founded? | Edinburgh | Paris | Rome | *London
exercise: In church and RE, what does salvation mean? | Going shopping on a Sunday | Having a loud brass band | *Being saved from sin and its results | Wearing a uniform to school
exercise: Mum says, «The bus was my salvation in the rain.» What does salvation mean here? | A type of church song | *Something that saved me from getting soaked | A rainy bus journey with no seats | A bus that was late
test: «The Salvation Army is famous for helping the poor.» What is the Salvation Army famous for? | Painting pictures | *Helping the poor | Racing cars
test: Which two people founded the Salvation Army? | *William and Catherine Booth | Martin and Anne Luther | Tom and Mary Clark | John and Sarah Wesley
exam: Which sentence uses salvation in the church sense? | *"Christians believe Jesus brings salvation, so that people can be close to God for ever." | "The late train was a disaster." | "The bus was my salvation in the rain." | "The rescue boat was our salvation at sea."
